Decision Workbench uses LangGraph (MIT) for its graph runtime.

The optional local model adapter uses DecisionTune 1.0 and decision-tune==1.0.0,
published by DecisionTune / hotin.ai under Apache-2.0.
Model: https://huggingface.co/decision-tune/decisiontune-1.0
Implementation: https://github.com/decision-tune/decision-tune
DecisionTune is based on answerdotai/ModernBERT-large. Its model card documents
additional training-data attribution and provenance limits. Model weights and
upstream implementation files are not redistributed in this repository.

The public-data comparison also loads these third-party checkpoints, without
redistributing their weights:
- Laya Multilingual by Convai Innovations and Laya contributors, Apache-2.0;
  independent FP16 MLX port by laya-mlx contributors, published by aac6fef,
  Apache-2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual
  https://huggingface.co/aac6fef/laya-multilingual-mlx
  Runtime: https://github.com/MohammadAsadi-7/laya-mlx (Apache-2.0)
- Qwen3-0.6B by the Qwen Team / Alibaba, Apache-2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B
  Loaded through Transformers (Apache-2.0) and PyTorch (BSD-style).

benchmarks/public-v1/cases.jsonl includes adapted selected test data from CUAD
(The Atticus Project; Hendrycks, Burns, Chen and Ball, 2021) and BANKING77
(PolyAI; Casanueva, Temcinas, Gerz, Henderson and Vulic, 2020), both CC-BY-4.0.
Their text/annotations retain that license, rather than our code's MIT license.
Source revisions, attribution, license links and adaptation details:
benchmarks/public-v1/README.md and docs/datasets.md.

